You can now finetune models directly on agent traces using TRL, including Claude Code, Codex, OpenClaw, Pi traces, and more. This development suggests we're approaching a standard stack for training agentic models.

@lhoestq: "Agent traces are the new fuel. Looking forward to announcing `trl` official support for agent traces for training, with `datasets` v5 coming out tomorrow. You can pick local, synthetic, or community traces to train your own specialized agent."

The upcoming `trl sft --dataset-name julien-c/synthtraces` command will facilitate this process.
